# MgmtApplyResidueStanding, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml — the rules file that
# mgmt-apply.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test rules`
# needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`.
# Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml
# under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would fail it.
#
# THE COPY CANNOT DRIFT SILENTLY: `devbox run exporter-self-test` reads the alert out of both files
# and asserts expr/for/labels/annotations are identical.
#
# Regenerate after editing the alert in prometheusrule.yaml:
#   yq '{"groups": [{"name": "github", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "MgmtApplyResidueStanding")]}]}' \
#     argocd/resources/github-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml
groups:
  - name: github
    rules:
      - alert: MgmtApplyResidueStanding
        expr: |-
          (github_mgmt_apply_refused == 1)
            and on (repo, context, subject)
          (time() - max by (repo, context, subject) (github_mgmt_apply_refused_since_timestamp)) > 86400
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: "The management box has been refusing {{ $labels.subject }} on {{ $labels.repo }} master for over a day"
          description: 'mgmt-apply has held a `{{ $labels.context }}` failure for `{{ $labels.subject }}` on {{ $labels.repo }} master for more than 24h. What ends one: a root or `stage 1` refusal (the security boundary included) ends at the next span the box applies, or when a human `mgmt-tf apply` stamps the baseline (the box then posts `baseline: stamped by a human apply`); an `ansible <group>` refusal ends when that group reads clean — at the next span touching it, or the hourly re-read the box runs after a hand converge. Check: the refused commit (since_sha) and its status text (`gh api repos/teststuffstash/{{ $labels.repo }}/commits/<sha>/status` — a STATUS, not a check-run); `journalctl -u mgmt-apply -n50` on 192.168.2.53 (the re-read lines name the group and what still differs); github_mgmt_apply_outside_addresses for a root. A root refusal RATCHETS: it does not stamp the baseline, so every later master commit adds its residue to the same pending apply. A human apply is `devbox run mgmt-tf -- plan` then `apply` — never `-target` on the main root (FU-248). If github_mgmt_apply_since_floored is 1 the age is a LOWER bound: the retained history holds no clearing verdict for the subject.'
